## Made
* I started working through my copy of [Crafting Interpreters](https://craftinginterpreters.com/)
this month, which has been a joy. Progress has been slow, both because I have to find good
chunks of time to work on it and because I'm implementing the interpreter(s) in `zig`
rather than `java`/`c`, but it is still a grand old time. Repo is [here](https://codeberg.org/garrettm/crafting-interpreters),
though it will probably sit idle for a good chunk of June as I am doing a lot of
travelling at the start of the month.

# Stuff I Only Sorta Did or Didn't Do
* I said last month that I wanted to completely avoid HackerNews, and I did *mostly* do
that. I did focus mostly on my RSS feeds this month, which was good, but there was
definitely the occasional visit to the orange site, particularly in the afternoons at work
while waiting for CI to run. Not nearly as much though, and I do feel like I did a decent
job avoidng things that I knew would make me feel bad, which was good.
* I also said that I wanted to do one of my long runs in another part of the Netherlands,
and sadly that did not come to fruition. Not for lack of trying, but other events
conspired to land on my calendar most Sundays, which meant that the window for taking a
train elsewhere was pretty small. I did at least do my 20k along a different path than I
normally go, so there was something.

# Stuff I'm Gonna Do in June
June is a big month of travel for me, so I don't have really any specific goals for it
other than for all my flights to go smoothly (which is largely outside of my control
anyway). I do want to work on practicing my Dutch a bit more regularly, so lots of time
sitting around in airports might be a boon there.
